{"name":"Superman Red","hex":"#ff1122","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"superman","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An imagined superior type of human being representing a new stage of human development; an übermensch; , a man of extraordinary powers. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Someone likened to the comics character Superman; a man of seemingly superhuman powers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superman"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Superman Red/Superman Blue","blocks":[{"text":"\"Superman Red/Superman Blue\" refers to two comic book storylines published by DC Comics featuring Superman."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b8/Supesredblue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superman_Red%2FSuperman_Blue"},{"title":"Superman","blocks":[{"text":"Superman is a superhero created by writer Jerry Siegel and artist Joe Shuster, first appearing in issue #1 of Action Comics, published in the United States on April 18, 1938. Superman has been regularly published in American comic books published by DC Comics since then, and has been adapted to other media including radio serials, novels, films, television shows, theater, and video games. Superman is the archetypal superhero: he wears an outlandish costume, uses a codename, and fights evil and averts disasters with the aid of extraordinary abilities. Although there are earlier characters who arguably fit this definition, it was Superman who popularized the superhero genre and established its conventions. He was the best-selling superhero in American comic books up until the 1980s and remains the highest grossing superhero if one considers the entire history of the genre."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/35/Supermanflying.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superman"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/65/Supesredblue.PNG/250px-Supesredblue.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/65/Supesredblue.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/65/Supesredblue.PNG/250px-Supesredblue.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Supergirl is introduced to Superman-Red and Superman-Blue, art by Curt Swan.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASupesredblue.PNG"},{"srcset":"